  <name>Rustab</name>
  <summary>Safely view, edit, and validate /etc/fstab</summary>

  <developer id="dev.tomsk">
    <name>Tomáš "tomsk" Sabo</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Rustab is a modern, native Linux desktop GUI for viewing, editing,
      adding, and removing entries in /etc/fstab, built with stability and
      data safety as the top priority.
    </p>
    <p>Rustab combines a clean, intuitive interface with a safety-first architecture:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full fstab syntax support: UUIDs, LABELs, device paths, network sources, bind mounts, swap entries, and systemd-generator options (x-systemd.*), with comments and formatting round-tripping perfectly</li>
      <li>Atomic writes and automatic timestamped backups on every save, with mandatory findmnt --verify validation before anything is written to disk</li>
      <li>A clear real-vs-sandbox target indicator and a mandatory diff review before saving, so every change is visible and reviewed before it persists</li>
      <li>Device and mount-point pickers to make entry creation easier, with graceful fallback to manual entry if the underlying system tools are unavailable</li>
      <li>A dev sandbox by default - pointing the app at the real /etc/fstab is an explicit, auditable choice, never the default</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Editing the real /etc/fstab requires administrator privileges and shows
      an explicit confirmation step; sandbox edits never require elevation.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">dev.tomsk.Rustab.desktop</launchable>

